commit 2b4c387f43874661f1890279862edf2d6e59ff9a
Author: Avijit Pal <palavijit713130@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Aug 9 01:30:30 2026 +0000

    fix(security): stop logging credentials and lock down the metrics endpoints
    
    1. Credentials were written to the logs on every request
       Several routes carry a credential in the query string: the email
       verification link (?token=), signed storage URLs (?token=&exp=) and the
       OAuth callback (?code=). Both the pino request serializer and the
       exception filter logged request.url verbatim, so those values landed in
       every access log and every error entry — retained by log aggregators
       and readable by anyone with log access. An email verification token is
       an account-takeover primitive for its full 24-hour lifetime.
    
       New redactUrl() masks a fixed list of sensitive parameter names while
       leaving the rest readable, so logs stay useful for debugging. Applied
       to the pino serializer, the exception filter's log line, and the error
       response body (which client-side error reporters routinely capture).
       Added a pino redact config for the authorization and cookie headers
       and for password/token bodies, so the protection survives someone
       widening the serializers later.
    
    2. Every 4xx logged a full stack trace at error level
       Validation failures, 401s and 404s all produced stack traces, which
       buries the 5xx that need attention and makes an unauthenticated 404
       flood a disk-space vector. Stacks are now kept for 5xx only, and 4xx
       log at warn.
    
    3. /api/metrics was completely unauthenticated
       No guard at all. /metrics/system returned host RAM, CPU load average
       and process uptime to any anonymous caller. /metrics/health returned
       raw driver error strings — connection targets, hostnames, file paths —
       whenever a dependency was down. Combined, a free reconnaissance
       surface.
    
       The controller now requires JwtAuthGuard + RolesGuard with
       @Roles(ADMIN), matching the existing admin metrics endpoint.
       ObservabilityModule imports AuthModule so the guards resolve;
       verified by booting the full AppModule.
    
       Health check messages are now generic ('Database unreachable' rather
       than the driver's text). The detail is still captured, via the logger,
       where operators can see it and callers cannot.
    
    If a Prometheus scraper needs unauthenticated access, bind it to an
    internal-only port rather than reopening these routes — noted in the
    controller.
    
    Tests: 12 cases in redact-url.spec.ts covering each credential-bearing
    route, case-insensitive matching, malformed percent-encoding, and that
    `tokenCount` is not over-redacted. Backend src suite 521 -> 533 passing;
    the 3 remaining failures are the pre-existing @nestjs/testing
    module-loading race, unchanged.

