    "CORS_ORIGIN === 'true'", a string that appears nowhere in the file, so
    it could never fail — the vulnerability sat behind a green check. It now
    asserts the absence of both fail-open branches and the presence of the
    explicit allowlist test.
    
    Verified: every combination of unset / empty / wildcard / configured
    against both production and development resolves as intended; tsc and
    the backend build are clean; src suite unchanged at 491 passing.

