commit 6045dbcfe646a3a81504f2808a871c23127a6527
Author: Avijit Pal <palavijit713130@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 10:46:25 2026 +0000

    fix: correct four defects found while reviewing the Phase 0 commits
    
    Self-review of the preceding six commits surfaced two mistakes I
    introduced and two pre-existing bugs that the new CI would not have
    caught. Fixing them here rather than amending, so the review trail
    stays visible.
    
    Introduced in "fix(api): correct auth refresh and retry semantics"
    1. getValidToken could attempt a refresh during SSR. The guard read
       `!stored && typeof window !== "undefined"`, so on the server (where
       the token store is deliberately inert and `stored` is always null)
       the early return did not fire and execution fell through to
       forceRefreshValidToken. It rejected immediately, so nothing broke,
       but every SSR request paid for a thrown-and-caught promise. Now
       returns null up front when there is no window.
    2. A 401 on anonymous traffic was treated as a session expiry. A
       logged-out visitor hitting any authenticated endpoint would trigger
       a refresh, fail, fire AUTH_EXPIRED_EVENT and get redirected to
       /auth. Requests now record whether an Authorization header was
       actually sent and only attempt recovery if there was a real session;
       otherwise the 401 surfaces as UNAUTHORIZED. Two regression tests
       added (22 tests total, up from 20).
    
    Introduced in "ci: make CI actually run"
    3. The release workflow could never trigger. It used workflow_run with
       `branches: [main]`, but that filter only matches branch refs, so a
       tag-triggered CI run never satisfies it. Releases would have
       silently stopped firing entirely. Replaced with a direct tag trigger
       plus an explicit wait on the Launch Gate check for that same commit,
       which enforces the same gate without the dead filter.
    
    Pre-existing
    4. The production container could not start. `nest build` was emitting
       dist/src/main.js, not dist/main.js, because seed-demo-data.ts sits
       outside src/ and widened the inferred rootDir to the package root.
       Both `CMD ["node", "dist/main"]` and the start:prod script pointed
       at a path that did not exist. Pinned rootDir to ./src and excluded
       the seed script from the build. Added a CI step asserting
       dist/main.js exists so this cannot regress silently.
    
       Also fixed the prod-deps Docker stage I added: it ran
       `npx prisma generate` after `npm install --omit=dev`, but `prisma`
       is a devDependency and would not have been present. The runtime
       image now copies the client the builder already generated
       (node_modules/.prisma and @prisma/client) after the prod-deps tree,
       so it is not overwritten.
    
    Also gitignore *.tsbuildinfo, which the backend build drops into the
    working tree.
    
    Verified: typecheck, lint (0 warnings), format, 22 tests and the
    frontend build all pass; backend builds and emits dist/main.js; both
    workflow files parse as valid YAML.
    
    Noted for later, not fixed here: public/icon-192.png and icon-512.png
    are 1x1 pixel placeholders declared as 192x192 and 512x512 in the web
    manifest, and public/og-image.png is actually a WebP file with a .png
    extension. Both are cosmetic/SEO issues for the polish phase.

