commit 0830dec06328fcb7952ec83e4468477973ec6a9c
Author: Avijit Pal <palavijit713130@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 10:18:57 2026 +0000

    ci: make CI actually run, and cover the frontend
    
    CI has never completed a single successful run. Every job began with
    "npm ci", but there is no package-lock.json anywhere in the repo (both
    workspaces use Bun and commit bun.lock), so all six jobs died on their
    first step. The launch-gate job, which is described as verifying
    production invariants, has therefore never executed.
    
    Worse, even a working CI would not have caught the two regressions
    fixed earlier in this branch: every job was scoped to apps/backend, so
    the 400-file frontend was never typechecked, linted, tested or built.
    
    Runner
    - Replace setup-node + npm ci with setup-bun + bun install
      --frozen-lockfile, matching the committed lockfiles. The backend test
      script is "bun test", which setup-node could never have provided.
    
    New frontend job
    - typecheck, lint, format check, unit tests and a production build.
      The build step is the one that catches bundler-only failures such as
      importing a .d.ts, which tsc cannot see.
    
    Gates that could not fail
    - "npm run format" ran prettier --write and "npm run lint" ran eslint
      --fix, so both repaired their own input and always exited 0. CI now
      runs prettier --check and eslint --max-warnings=0.
    - The docker job ran "docker run ... --help || true", discarding every
      failure. It now asserts dist/main.js exists in the image and that no
      .env was baked in.
    - Removed five brittle grep assertions from the security job. One of
      them (onClick={onOpenSearch} in MobileNav.tsx) matches current code
      and would have failed the build; it was stale from an old refactor.
      Product behaviour belongs in tests, not string matching.
    - launch-gate now also verifies both .dockerignore files exclude .env
      and that no compose file defaults a secret to a known value.
    
    Frontend test infrastructure
    - The test script pointed at --dir src while all component tests live in
      tests/, so "no test files found" and the 6 suites had never run. They
      also could not have run: @testing-library/react and jsdom were never
      installed. Added those plus @testing-library/user-event.
    - Added vitest.config.ts, kept separate from vite.config.ts because the
      latter pulls in TanStack Start, Nitro and PWA plugins that drag the
      backend workspace into test runs. It excludes apps/** since the
      backend uses bun:test, which vitest cannot resolve.
    - tests/setup.ts: polyfill IntersectionObserver, ResizeObserver,
      matchMedia and scrollIntoView (jsdom lacks them and motion throws
      without them), and register RTL cleanup, which only auto-registers
      under globals: true and was silently leaking DOM between tests.
    - Repaired three suites that were broken against current code:
      MemoryStreaks imported a deleted module, CalendarHero needed its React
      Query hooks stubbed, and JournalEntryCard asserted on content that the
      first card renders twice.
    
    Result: 20 tests across 6 files now run and pass, up from zero.
    
    Also: scope eslint and prettier to project source. They were walking
    .local/skills (vendored third-party code, 5,249 of the 7,979 reported
    issues) and apps/, which has its own config. Disable the react-refresh
    rule for shadcn ui files, the actions list and the context modules,
    where co-locating a component with its variants or hook is the intended
    pattern and the rule only affects dev-server HMR.
    
    Release workflow
    - It triggered directly on a tag push with no dependency on CI, so a tag
      on an unverified commit could publish an image to GHCR. It now runs on
      workflow_run after CI succeeds, with a manual dispatch escape hatch.
    - Added environment: production for approval and audit, a concurrency
      group so two releases cannot race, and cache-from/to.
    - :latest now moves only for a clean semver tag, so a hotfix or
      pre-release cut from an older commit cannot overwrite it.
    - Pinned trufflehog (was tracking @main, an unpinned moving branch with
      repo access) and upgraded the deprecated action-gh-release v1 and
      build-push-action v5.
    - Added concurrency and caching to CI; four jobs each cold-installed
      ~600 MB on every run.
    
    Verified locally: typecheck, lint:ci, format:check, test and build all
    exit 0.

