commit dad2ab7f579fc86c155a2ed52d949d56deca566a
Author: Avijit Pal <palavijit713130@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 09:25:31 2026 +0000

    fix: repair broken production build and Rules of Hooks violation
    
    Two regressions from 473f899 that together made the app undeployable and
    crashed the library page. Neither was caught locally because CI has never
    run (no package-lock.json for 'npm ci') and 'tsc --noEmit' passes on both.
    
    1. Build failure — src/lib/analytics.ts
       'import "./types/global"' resolved to global.d.ts, an ambient
       declaration file with no runtime output. TypeScript accepts it; the
       bundler cannot emit it, so 'vite build' died with:
         [UNRESOLVED_IMPORT] Could not resolve './types/global'
       The Window augmentation already applies globally via tsconfig
       'include', so the import was never needed. Removed, with a comment so
       it is not reintroduced.
    
       Also replaced the three empty catch blocks with a dev-only warn. A
       silently dead analytics pipeline is indistinguishable from an
       unconfigured one, and 'no-empty' was erroring in lint.
    
    2. Rendered fewer hooks than expected — src/routes/app.library.all.tsx
       The isError/isLoading early returns were inserted above useMemo,
       two useRefs and useEffect. React identifies hooks by call order, so
       the hook count changed from 0 to 4 across the loading -> loaded
       transition and React threw, blanking the page behind the error
       boundary. Moved both returns below every hook.
    
       Also fixed '(m.rating ?? 0) ?? 0' (no-constant-binary-expression).
    
    Verified: 'bun run build' exits 0 and emits dist/ + .output/;
    'tsc --noEmit' clean; no rules-of-hooks or no-empty errors remain in
    the touched files.

