commit 5f0f8f8fb81ec783262d941afbd28bd8194ea1c9
Author: Avijit Pal <palavijit713130@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 09:12:19 2026 +0000

    chore: enforce LF line endings via .gitattributes and .editorconfig
    
    The repo had no .gitattributes and core.autocrlf was unset, leaving 644
    files LF-in-index but CRLF-in-worktree and 48 files with mixed endings
    inside a single file. A clean 'git diff' reported 58,849 changed lines
    of which only ~146 were real code (0.26%), making every diff, PR review
    and 'git blame' unusable.
    
    - .gitattributes: '* text=auto eol=lf' as the single source of truth so
      the rule travels with the repo and binds contributors and CI alike
      (core.autocrlf is machine-local and does neither). Windows scripts
      keep CRLF; binaries are marked so Git never rewrites them; lockfiles
      and routeTree.gen.ts are marked -diff linguist-generated.
    - .editorconfig: matching end_of_line=lf so editors stop reintroducing
      CRLF on save.
    - .prettierrc: add explicit endOfLine 'lf'. The root config omitted it
      while apps/backend/.prettierrc already set it, so the two disagreed
      and ESLint (prettier/prettier: error) would have fought Git.
    
    Also set core.fileMode=false locally: WSL on NTFS was reporting a
    spurious 100644 -> 100755 flip on all 1,130 tracked files.

